    "campaign": "DEC IG & FB",
    "caption": "Make these mouthwatering Chicken Karaage Sliders, complete with a sumptuous Asian slaw, with Betagro Chicken Karaage!\n\nThere’s nothing like a fried chicken sandwich to provide comfort after a long day, and because Betagro Chicken Karaage comes seasoned and ready to fry, there’s no need to busy yourself too much in the kitchen! Perfect as an after work indulgence or entertaining with friends, these sliders will surely be the talk of the town. The Asian slaw packs heaps of flavor thanks to the umami-filled mix of vinegar, soy sauce, and sesame oil. Enjoy! Head over to #TheMarketplace and find all the ingredients that you need for this recipe.\n\nServing Time: 25-30 minutes\nYield: 6-8 servings\n\nIngredients\n\noil for frying\n1 pack Betagro Chicken Karaage\n\nFor the slaw:\n1 cup purple cabbage, shredded\n1 cup green cabbage, shredded\n½ cup shredded carrot\n⅓ cup mayonnaise\n2 tbsps. rice vinegar\n1 tbsp. soy sauce\n1 tsp. sesame oil\n1 tbsp. honey\nSalt and pepper to taste\n\nFor the sliders:\n12 dinner rolls\n½ cup pickle, sliced\n\nProcedure\nHeat a large pot of oil over medium-high heat or until it reaches 170°C..\nFry Betagro Chicken Karaage in batches until golden brown and crispy, about 3-4 minutes per batch.\nDrain the chicken on a paper towel-lined plate.\nTo make the slaw, In a medium bowl, combine the cabbage, carrot, mayonnaise, rice vinegar, soy sauce, sesame oil, and honey. Season with salt and pepper.\nToss to coat and let the slaw sit for 15 minutes before using.\nTo assemble the sliders, toast the slider buns.\nPlace about a tablespoon of slaw. Top with a piece of chicken karaage and sliced pickle.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
