    "caption": "Prepare something sweet and special this holiday season by baking this delicious Cappuccino Cake using Bon Aroma Roast Master Brazil Coffee!\n\nBold, delicious, and bursting with the flavors of coffee, add a personal touch to your holiday dinner spread or holiday gifting with this fantastic cake. Did we forget to mention that the coffee buttercream is equally addictive? The secret to bringing out the flavors of the coffee is a dash of salt, which lifts the nuances and notes of this robust Brazilian coffee from Bon Aroma. Grab your stash at #TheMarketplace, and don’t forget to serve this luscious cake with Bon Aroma coffee, too!\n\nServing Time: 2 hours\nYield: 8 servings\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the Cake:\n2 ¼ cups all-purpose flour \n2 tbsps. Bon Aroma Roast Master Brazil Coffee\n¼ tsp. salt\n½ cup unsalted butter, softened\n1 ½ cups granulated sugar\n3 large eggs, at room temperature\n1 ½ tbsps. vanilla extract\n1 cup buttermilk, at room temperature\n\nFor the Coffee Buttercream:\n2 tbsps. Bon Aroma Roast Master Brazil Coffee\n1 tbsp. hot water\n2 tbsp. cold water \n1 cup unsalted butter, softened\n3 cups powdered sugar\n1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n½ cup chocolate shavings\n\nProcedure\nPreheat the oven to 175°C. Grease and flour two 9-inch round cake pans.\nIn a medium bowl, whisk together the flour, Bon Aroma Roast Master Brazil Coffee, and salt. Set aside.\nIn a large bowl, cream together the butter and sugar until light and fluffy. Beat in the eggs one at a time, then stir in the vanilla extract.\nAlternately add the dry ingredients and the buttermilk to the butter mixture, beginning and ending with the dry ingredients. Mix until just combined.\nBake for 25-30 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.\nLet the cakes cool in the pans for 10 minutes before inverting them onto wire racks to cool completely.\nDissolve Bon Aroma Roast Master Brazil Coffee in hot water. Once dissolved add cold water\nIn a large bowl, beat the butter until light and fluffy.\nGradually add the powdered sugar, beating until smooth.\nBeat in the coffee and vanilla extract until combined.\nSpread the coffee buttercream and top with chocolate shavings.\nChill for about an hour before serving.\n\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
