    "campaign": "DEC IG & FB",
    "caption": "Intimidated by the oven but keen to make a sweet treat this festive season?\n\nHead over to #TheMarketplace and grab packets of M.Y. San Graham Crackers and make this No Bake Eclair Cake! Think of it as a fancier and chocolatier spin of the popular fruit dessert floats, but what makes this dessert special is the homemade pastry cream that’s bursting with vanilla flavors. Make it even fancier by adding some actual vanilla beans while folding the cream! Chuck it in the fridge at least an hour before serving, and you’ve got yourself a solid dessert that everyone will surely enjoy.\n\nServing Time: 3 hours and 40 minutes\nYield: 10-12 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n1 cup whole milk\n¼ cup granulated sugar\n¼ cup cornstarch\n3 large egg yolks\n2 tbsps. unsalted butter, softened\n1 tsp. vanilla extract \n2 cups heavy cream\n2 tbsps. powdered sugar\n½ tsp. vanilla extract\n1 pack M.Y. San Graham Crackers \n1 cup semisweet chocolate, chopped\n¼ cup M.Y. San Graham Crackers, crushed\n\nProcedure\nMake the pastry cream: In a medium saucepan, whisk together the milk, sugar, and cornstarch. Cook over medium heat, whisking constantly, until the mixture thickens and comes to a boil. Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 1 minute, whisking constantly. \nRemove the saucepan from the heat and whisk in the egg yolks one at a time. Whisk until the mixture is smooth.\nStir in the butter and vanilla extract until the butter is melted and smooth. \nPour the pastry cream into a medium bowl and cover the surface with plastic wrap. Refrigerate for at least 2 hours, or until chilled.\nMake the whipped cream: In a large bowl, whip the 1 cup  heavy cream, powdered sugar, and vanilla extract until stiff peaks form.\nFold the whipped cream into the pastry cream: Once the pastry cream is chilled, add ⅓ of the whipped cream to the bowl and fold gently until combined. Add the remaining whipped cream and fold until just combined\nLine a 8x8-inch pan with a single layer of M.Y. San Graham Crackers. Spread half of the diplomat cream over the graham crackers.\nAdd another layer of graham crackers. Spread the remaining diplomat cream over the graham crackers.\nTop with a final layer of graham crackers. Cover the pan with plastic wrap and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes.\nIn a medium saucepan, heat the remaining 1 cup  heavy cream over medium heat until it just begins to simmer. Do not let it boil.\nRemove the saucepan from the heat and immediately pour the hot cream over the chopped chocolate in a heatproof bowl.\nLet the chocolate sit in the hot cream for 5 minutes, then stir gently until the chocolate is completely melted and the ganache is smooth and glossy.\nSpread the chocolate ganache over the top of the cake and sprinkle crushed grahams. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour before serving.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
