    "campaign": "DEC IG & FB",
    "caption": "The holiday season is a great reason to indulge in all things rich and decadent.\n\nFor Christmas breakfast, whip up this Croissant French Toast with super buttery slices of Elsie’s Croissants. Dredge your croissant slices in a simple egg bath, fry, top with a dollop of whipped cream, and sprinkle with juicy berries. Drizzle your favorite maple sauce (or honey) on top, or add a sweeter touch and serve with some caramel sauce and fruit compote on the side. Need we say more? Don’t forget to make a trip to #TheMarketplace and gather all your holiday essentials there!\n\nServing Time: 15 minutes  \nYield: 2 servings \n\nIngredients\n\n3 large eggs\n1 cup whole milk\n1/4 cup maple syrup\n1 tsp. vanilla extract\n1/4 tsp. ground cinnamon\nPinch of salt\n2 pcs. Elsies Croissants, sliced \n2 tbsps. butter\n1/2 cup heavy cream, whipped\n1 cup fresh strawberries, hulled and halved\n1/2 cup fresh blueberries\n\nProcedure\nIn a large shallow bowl, whisk together eggs, milk, maple syrup, vanilla extract, cinnamon, and salt.\nDip each Elsies Croissant slice into the egg mixture, coating both sides evenly.\nHeat a large skillet over medium heat, and melt butter. Add the soaked croissant slices into the skillet, and cook for 2-3 minutes per side, or until golden brown.\nTo assemble the french toast, place a croissant slice on a serving plate. Top with a dollop of whipped cream, strawberries, and blueberries. \nDrizzle with additional maple syrup, if desired.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
