    "campaign": "DEC IG & FB",
    "caption": "Menbosha, or shrimp toast, is a popular snack in Cantonese cuisine.\n\nHot and crispy on the outside and chewy on the inside, this recipe uses Gardenia White Bread and a simple shrimp filling that’s flavored with chicken stock, lemon juice, and nutty sesame oil. Deep-fried to a shattering crunch, these delectable bites will surely be a hit at any canapé spread. Make sure to prepare extra batches because these will disappear quick! Make a trip to #TheMarketplace soon and find everything you need to make these delicious bite-sized shrimp toast sandwiches.\n\nServing Time: 30 minutes \nYield: 9-10 servings \n\nIngredients\n\n12 slices Gardenia White Bread\n300g shrimp, peeled and deveined\n2 tbsps. cornstarch\n1 egg white\n1 tsp. chicken stock \n1 tbsp. lemon juice\n1 tbsp. sesame oil\nSalt and pepper to taste\nVegetable oil for deep frying\n\nProcedure\nSlice off the crusts from the Gardenia White Bread. Slice into 4. \nIn a food processor, pulse the shrimp until finely chopped.\nTransfer the shrimp into a bowl, then mix in the cornstarch, egg white, chicken stock, lemon juice, sesame oil oil, salt, and pepper. Mix well until the ingredients are evenly distributed.\nSpread a thin layer of shrimp mixture on each slice of Gardenia White Bread. Freeze for 15 minutes. \nHeat vegetable oil in a deep fryer, or large pot to 175°C.\nFry sandwiches for 2-3 minutes, or until bread is golden brown and shrimp is cooked through. \nRemove the bread slices from the oil, then drain on a paper towel-lined plate.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
