    "campaign": "DEC IG & FB",
    "caption": "Jazz up your caprese salad with some bell peppers! Not to mention, they add some gorgeous colors to the platter, too.\n\nGrab some fresh bell peppers at #TheMarketplace, roast them to bring out their sweetness, and assemble with some mozzarella cheese, basil leaves, and a generous swig of Monini Extra Virgin Olive Oil. As with most salads, the dressing is such an important component, so we’ve made an olive oil vinaigrette with base ingredients of balsamic vinegar, shallots, and mustard, which is so versatile, you can use it with your other salad creations as well. We hope you enjoy making this delightful starter as much as you enjoy eating it!\n\nServing Time: 45 minutes \nYield: 1-2 servings \n\nIngredients\n3 bell peppers, deseeded and sliced\n2 tbsps. Monini Extra Virgin Olive Oil\nSalt and pepper to taste\n1 pound fresh mozzarella cheese, sliced \n1/4 cup fresh basil leaves\n\nFor the Vinaigrette: \n1/4 cup extra virgin olive oil\n2 tbsps. balsamic vinegar\n1 tsp. Dijon mustard\n1 shallot, minced\nSalt and pepper to taste\n\nProcedure\nPreheat oven to 200C. Place bell pepper halves on a baking sheet, and drizzle with Monini Extra Virgin Olive Oil. Season with salt and pepper. Roast for 20-25 minutes, or until the peppers are tender and slightly charred.\nTo assemble the salad, arrange the mozzarella slices on a platter. Top with the roasted pepper strips and basil leaves.\nTo make the vinaigrette, whisk together the Monini Extra Virgin Olive Oil, balsamic vinegar, Dijon mustard, shallot, salt and pepper in a small bowl.\nDrizzle the vinaigrette over the salad and serve immediately.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
