    "caption": "Obsessed with avocados? We are, too!\n\nToday, we’ll show you how to make an Avocado Vinaigrette using Valencia Avocado Oil, which works perfectly with absolutely any salad. And as a bonus, we’ll also put together a simple salad with — you guessed it — more avocado, along with some mixed lettuce and chickpeas.\n\nAvocados are known to be nutrient-dense fruits that come with a lot of health benefits in tow such as vitamin E, potassium, magnesium, and folate. Enjoy this fiber-rich salad on its own or serve with your favorite protein. Find Valencia Avocado Oil, along with the freshest avocados, at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 12 minutes \nYield: 1-2 servings \n\nIngredients\n\nFor the Avocado Vinaigrette:\n1 ripe avocado, pitted\n¼ cup Valencia Avocado Oil\n2 tbsps. lemon juice\n1 tbsp. Dijon mustard\n½ ttsp. Honey\nSalt and pepper to taste\n\nFor the Salad: \n1 ripe avocado, pitted and sliced \n1 red onion, sliced\n3 cups mixed lettuce\n½ cup chickpeas, drained \nSalt and pepper to taste\n\nProcedure\nIn a blender, combine the avocado, Valencia Avocado Oil, lemon juice, Dijon mustard, and honey. Blend until smooth and creamy. Season with salt and pepper to taste.\nIn a large bowl, combine the avocado, onions, lettuce and chickpeas. \nDrizzle with the avocado vinaigrette and toss to coat. Season with salt and pepper to taste.\nServe immediately, or chill for later.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
