    "caption": "In the mood for a light, delicious, and fiber-packed meal to nosh on in between your indulgent holiday gatherings?\n\nGrab a loaf of Gardenia High Fiber Whole Wheat Bread on your next grocery run at #TheMarketplace, and prepare these Creamy Mushroom Toasts that make for a light and filling meal or snack, without compromising on flavor. In fact, it packs a strong punch of umami thanks to the two types of mushroom used, along with a spread of cream cheese and some lettuce to boot. Pack this along for lunch in the office, together with your favorite sliced fruit or vegetable sticks with a side of ranch or bleu cheese dressing!\n\nServing Time: 15 minutes\nYield: 2 servings\n\nIngredients\n⅛ cup olive oil\n1 cup shiimeji mushroom, pulled apart\n1 cup button mushroom, sliced\nSalt and pepper to taste \n4 slices Gardenia High Fiber Whole Wheat Bread\n1 cup cream cheese\n1 cup mizuna lettuce\n1/2 tbsp. chili flakes\n\nProcedure\nHeat olive oil in a pan over medium heat. Add the mushrooms, and cook until softened and nicely browned, about 5 minutes. Season with salt and pepper. Set aside.\nToast Gardenia High Fiber Whole Wheat Bread until crisp. Spread cream cheese on each slice of bread.\nTop the toast with mizuna lettuce, cooked mushrooms and chili flakes.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
