    "caption": "Rich, creamy, and packed with the robust flavors of cheese, potatoes, and Harvest Applewood Smoked Sliced Bacon, this Loaded Baked Potato Soup is the perfect dish to nosh on to keep you warm on a chilly December day, or if you’ve had way too many drinks the night before.\n\nCozy, soul-warming, and extremely hearty, this satisfying soup will surely be a mainstay on your recipe rolodex — even after the holiday season. Great to slurp on when you’re in need of some comfort, this is one dish that feels like a big hug. Add more love to it by making this soup for your family and friends to enjoy as well. Get all the ingredients that you need at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 30 minutes\nYield: 4-5 servings\n\nIngredients\n12 slices Harvest Applewood Smoked Sliced Bacon, diced\n2 tbsps. butter\n1 cup white onion, chopped \n¼ cup all-purpose flour\n6 cups chicken broth\n3 cups potatoes, peeled and cubed\n1 ½ cup heavy cream\n1 tsp. salt\n½ tsp. black pepper\n¼ cup sour cream\n¼ cup green onions, chopped\n½ cup cheddar cheese, shredded\n\nProcedure\nIn a large pot, fry Harvest Applewood Smoked Sliced Bacon until crisp. Set aside while retaining about 1 tbsp. of bacon fat. \nAdd butter and white onions, then sauté until translucent. Mix in flour, and cook for about 1 minute.\nGradually whisk in the chicken broth. Add potatoes and let simmer for 15 minutes or until potatoes are tender.\nAdd heavy cream and half of crispy Harvest Applewood Smoked Sliced Bacon. Season with salt and pepper.  \nTransfer to a soup bowl. Top each serving with a dollop of sour cream, crispy Harvest Applewood Smoked Sliced Bacon, green onions and cheddar cheese.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
